The software architecture of a system is a high-level description of a system's structure . its different components, and how those components communicate with each other to fulfill the systems requirements and constrains
      High-Level systems structure - Technologies , progamming langueges not part of the architecture but part of the implementation stage
                                   -  Decisions about implementation should be delayed to teh very end of the design
      components       - Black box elements defined by their behavior and API's
                       - components may be complex systems with their own software architecture diagrams
      communication    - protocols used by the components internally and externally
      requirements     - components come together to do what the systems is intended to do as required
      constrains       - system does not what it shouldn't do 

